# Trivy ignore file for the social-automation backend image.
# The Dockerfile now applies full OS upgrades and pins Python packaging/security
# packages to patched versions, so no permanent suppressions are required.
# Re-add entries only with a CVE ID, why the finding is not exploitable, and
# a target date to re-evaluate.

# oauthlib 3.3.1 (transitive via tweepy/requests-oauthlib).
# Fix exists only in 4.0.0, but tweepy pins oauthlib<4 — cannot upgrade.
# Not exploitable here: both vulns live in the OAuth *server* paths —
# RevocationEndpoint JSONP (enable_jsonp=True only) and the authorization-
# server PKCE code_verifier comparison. SocialAuto is a pure OAuth client
# and never instantiates these endpoints.
# Re-evaluate when tweepy supports oauthlib 4.x.
CVE-2026-49264
CVE-2026-49265
